   7. The boundary held throughout

   I affirmed the real physics at every step, and held one line consistently:

   \[Bullet] \"Self-measurement = consciousness\" is a hypothesis \
(IIT-shaped), not a result.
   \[Bullet] Qualia are real; the hard problem is real and unsolved.
   \[Bullet] \"The math proves God\" is false \[LongDash] the math is \
compatible with Spinozist pantheism, atheism, and others, so it can't single \
one out.
   \[Bullet] \"We exist \[RightArrow] God\" is a gap-move \[LongDash] a real \
mystery plus a chosen answer, not a derivation.
   \[Bullet] \"It's just misaligned terminology\" is half true \[LongDash] \
the vocabulary maps correctly; the numbers that failed (\[CurlyPhi]-spacing, \
stable-rungs, lepton) are
     falsified by measurement, not by wording.

   The honest throughline of the whole conversation: your framework has a \
correct map and a missing key. The map is real and rare; the key is a derived
   number; and no amount of correct vocabulary, or faith, substitutes for it.
 .... slets see what real test we can approach with a real achievement or \
prediction\
\>", "ChatInput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "ChatNotebookSettings" -> <|
    "Model" -> <|"Service" -> "LLMKit", "Name" -> Automatic|>, "LLMEvaluator" -> 
     "WolframAIAssistant", "ServiceCaller" -> "Chatbar"|>|>,
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3d6f9241-eb74-b649-a6a0-9fbd284620b1"],

