c^3 a)/(4 hbar g);\\nmargolusLevitin = e == (Pi hbar)/(2 \
tau);\\nsphericalArea = a == 4 Pi r^2;\\nlightCrossing = tau == \
r/c;\\n\\nstep1 = Solve[{bekenstein, holographic}, g][[1]] // \
Simplify\\nstep2 = Solve[{bekenstein, holographic, sphericalArea}, g][[1]] // \
Simplify\\nstep3 = Solve[{bekenstein, holographic, sphericalArea, \
margolusLevitin}, g][[1]] // Simplify\\nstep4 = Solve[{bekenstein, \
holographic, sphericalArea, margolusLevitin, lightCrossing}, g][[1]] // \
Simplify\\n```\\n\\nExpected symbolic outputs:\\n\\n```wl\\n(* step1 *)\\n g \
-> (a c^4)/(8 Pi e r)\\n\\n(* step2 *)\\n g -> (c^4 r)/(2 e)\\n\\n(* step3 *)\
\\n g -> (c^4 r tau)/(Pi hbar)\\n\\n(* step4 *)\\n g -> (c^3 r^2)/(Pi \
hbar)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Section 10. What this notebook is for\\n\\nThis \
notebook should now serve as the **foundation** for a larger RHUFT research \
notebook that does three things:\\n\\n1. audits additional RHUFT documents on \
the desktop,\\n2. extracts all candidate closure principles,\\n3. tests them \
one by one against the no-circularity criteria.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Final \
current conclusion\\n\\nAt present, Test 1 does **not** derive \
$$G$$.\\n\\nWhat it does provide is a clean, rigorous checkpoint:\\n\\n* the \
triad is mathematically coherent,\\n* the direct combination yields explicit \
consistency relations,\\n* the missing ingredient is now sharply \
identified,\\n* and the next stage is a targeted search for a true RHUFT \
closure postulate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Next notebook extension \
requested\\n\\nThe next rigorous extension should be:\\n\\n> **RHUFT Test 1B \
\[LongDash] Desktop-wide extraction and classification of candidate closure \
principles relevant to deriving $$G$$**\\n\\nThat extension should ingest \
RHUFT notebooks, markdown files, audits, and scale documents from the Desktop \
and adjacent RHUFT folders, then build a candidate table with:\\n\\n* source \
file\\n* exact quote\\n* symbolic form\\n* dimensional status\\n* circularity \
risk\\n* admissibility for Test 1\\n* recommended next action\"\>",
